  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">English &amp; School Education: School Systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme outcomes: &#x25FC; 1. Teachers and teacher educators demonstrate knowledge, skills and confidence to build learners&#x2019; English and core skills.&#x25FC; 2. School leaders and leadership teams create and sustain an enabling and safe environment for inclusive teaching and learning.&#x25FC; 3. Policy makers support and develop inclusive, quality education practice for language in education, English and core skills.&#x25FC; 4. Practitioners, policy makers and suppliers use evidence to create safe learning spaces, and inform practice, decision-making and course/resources design.&#x25FC; 5. Assessment, curriculum and resources to support language learning and core skills are fit for purpose and context appropriate.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">School Systems is one of the Global Programmes through which the British Council delivers its grant-funded activity. The primary focus of this Global Programme is ODA eligible activity and outcomes.The School Systems programme supports sustainable improvements to the quality of basic education in schools for all, in relation to English and core skills.What we do:&#x25FC;Convene and engage policy makers to support policy design and implementation.&#x25FC;Develop and disseminate research and evaluation.&#x25FC; Design and implement professional development programmes / opportunities for practitioners.&#x25FC;Provide technical assistance for the development of assessment, curricula and resources.&#x25FC; Focus on the priority themes of language in foundational learning, English in education, teaching quality, school leadership, girls&#x2019; education and life skills for young people.Why we do it:&#x25FC;More effective, inclusive and globally connected education systems in a linguistically rich and diverse world.&#x25FC;More equitable learning outcomes enabled for all young people in relation to English and core skills.&#x25FC;Sound and sustainable curricula, assessment and professional development for educators.&#x25FC; Mutually beneficial relationships built between the UK and countries worldwide to explore policy and develop practice in relation to English and school education.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The audiences for this programme are:&#x25FC; Teacher educators, teachers, school leaders and leadership teams.&#x25FC;Policymakers and decisionmakers, government officials.&#x25FC;Partners and funders.</narrative>
  </description>
